  <h2 id="roles-at-a-glance">What careers can you get with a behavioral psychology degree?</h2>
  <p>Behavioral psychology graduates work far beyond the therapist's office. The degree teaches you how to study behavior scientifically: designing studies, collecting data, and drawing evidence-based conclusions. Employers across research, education, business, and health value that skill set. The table below summarizes the most common roles, the degree each usually requires, and typical pay.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Typical setting</th><th scope="col">Usual degree</th><th scope="col">Typical salary range</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
